`CLAUDE.md` is compacted (`9cd56be21`), from 86 lines down to 50.

- **Kept:** where the repository comes from, the project goal with the pointers to the plan, handover and ledger, the layout, and the note that the 2012 READMEs describe their era.
- **New:** two pointers. Every agent loads `fortress-repo` before any work, and `remote-container` for the container. The coordinating session boots by the coordinator README and works by the `coordinator` skill.
- **Moved into `fortress-repo` only:**
  - the build and run commands, plus the install line, which the skill lacked;
  - the toolchain traps;
  - the "facts that save time", with `mandelbrot_canonical.fss` as the smoke test.
- **Dropped:**
  - the two lines telling agents to wipe the caches, which contradicted the never-wipe rule;
  - the line telling every agent to read the protocol at session start;
  - the Working Draft's conflicting date;
  - your name in the rules. The file now says "the curator (@palimondo)".
- **Left for the tuning after the boot:** the skills' source lists still cite the old `CLAUDE.md` text. The boot note has it.

Ready for compaction.

`CLAUDE.md` is up for review, with a comment on any paragraph or line: https://claude.ai/artifact/Xn31FRo3USai9SMutzMHiS

To get it there, I unwatched an old page from 09-26, because the session can watch only ten artifacts at a time.

I agree it can be a few lines. Every agent reads it on every start, and the skills now carry what it used to hold. My guess at what has to stay:
- one line on what the repository is;
- which skill to load when;
- the original tree is the historical artifact;
- copyrighted decks are never committed.

The project goal and the pointers to the plan, handover and ledger could move into the `coordinator` skill, since workers get them through their briefs. Your comments decide it. I'll make the changes as they come, or after the boot if you compact first.

I've added the missing items to the skills and fixed the three disagreements. Everything is committed and pushed (`26cfb123e`).

**Added:**
- **`coordinator` skill:**
  - how I handle your comments on a page;
  - the combined review after every landed batch;
  - a pointer to the batch manual for the mission briefing;
  - that you aren't reminded about the `wip/` branches;
  - the boot note's process start and next stop;
  - citing a FACTS entry with no title by its opening words.
- **`fortress-repo` skill:**
  - `main` is pushed right after every commit;
  - the same citation rule for an untitled FACTS entry.
- **`remote-container` skill:** a skill written mid-session shows up at once, with no restart.

**Fixed:**
- **The protocol's test-first rule** now matches POSITIONS: the test and the fix may land in one commit, and the skeptic reads the order from the worker's transcript instead of re-running it.
- **`committing.md`** gives the commit footer without pointing at the protocol.
- **`remote-container`** now says the git-check hook is on after every restart, and that turning it off is yours to do in manual mode.

The five tests for a consequential decision are still only in the skill and wait for your word. The boot note records all of this, so we can pick up from there later.

I've published the review page with all three skills, every part in full: https://claude.ai/artifact/Deuc1PeTurWDLqo2KCAPSp

It's the same layout as before, with a new link; the old page is unchanged. The box at the top covers:
- what changed since the last version, from comparing the skills with the boot records;
- the five tests for a consequential decision, which wait for your word;
- what is still open: retiring the protocol, and the batch script's field for points put to you.

Comment on any line and I'll answer on the thread and change the skill. The watch on this page is still being set up, and this session can watch at most ten pages, so if a comment doesn't reach me, mention it here.

I've started a fresh Fable worker. It's reading what I read at boot (`CLAUDE.md`, the protocol, the README, FACTS, POSITIONS, INDEX, the handover's first section, the boot note), then every file of the three skills.

I took your request to mean the worker both reviews and edits. It changes only the skill files, commits nothing, and writes its report to `explorations/reviews/skills-review-fable.md`. When it finishes, I'll:
- check its changes against POSITIONS;
- commit the skills and the report;
- update the review page at the same link;
- give you a short summary. Any decisions it took, or changes it held back because they would go against a position of yours, will come to you one at a time.

**Cost:** I estimate 0.5M to 1M tokens written on the Fable tier, about 300K of it just loading that context. That is a guess, not a measurement.

Messages to me are safe while it runs, but pressing stop on a turn would kill it.

